    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$60$",
      "worked": "The combined amount stays the same. Express both ratios with a total of 21 parts.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Original Tim:Luke} &= 15:6 \\\\\n\\text{New Tim:Luke} &= 14:7\n\\end{align*}$$\nLuke gains one part, so one part is worth $\\$10$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Luke's original amount} &= 6\\times\\$10 \\\\\n&= \\$60\n\\end{align*}$$",
